 <p>Lamine Yamal Nasraoui Ebana, commonly known as Lamine Yamal, is a Spanish professional footballer who has rapidly become one of the brightest young talents in world football. He was born on July 13, 2007, in Esplugues de Llobregat, near Barcelona, Spain, to a Moroccan father and an Equatorial Guinean mother. Yamal joined FC Barcelona’s famed La Masia academy at a very young age, where his exceptional technical skills, creativity, and maturity on the ball quickly set him apart from his peers. In April 2023, at just 15 years old, he made his senior debut for Barcelona, becoming one of the youngest players ever to appear for the club. Known for his pace, dribbling ability, and football intelligence, Yamal primarily plays as a right winger but is versatile across the attacking line. His performances for both club and country have drawn widespread acclaim, and in 2023 he made history by becoming the youngest player and goal scorer in the history of the Spanish national team. Widely regarded as a generational talent, Lamine Yamal is seen as the future of both FC Barcelona and Spanish football.</p>


